      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. Rewrote READI410_SVE_2X and the other 2x read macros to process the two vectors consecutively rather than interleaved (per your suggestion on line 1115), using consecutive ld1h / widening ld1b/ld1h/ld1w loads ([%[src]] with p1/z and [%[src], #1, mul vl] with p2/z) + in-lane trn1/trn2 instead of de-interleaving with ld2h or uzp1/uzp2. On I410ToARGB_Opt / I410ToAR30_Opt / I410AlphaToARGB_Opt, this improves performance vs Patch Set 1 by +11.4% to +15.3% on Cortex-A510 (SVE2), +12.3% to +14.6% on Oryon V3 (SME2), +1.7% to +14.1% on Apple M6 (SME2), and 3.40x-4.47x on Lumex C2-Ultra (SME2).",
