        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1115898
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-02T18:23:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. Rewrote all 2x YUV-to-RGB kernels (READYUV444_SVE_2X, READYUV400_SVE_2X, READYUV422_SVE_2X, READI210_SVE_2X, READP210_SVE_2X, READI410_SVE_2X, READI212_SVE_2X, READNV_SVE_2X, READYUY2_SVE_2X, READUYVY_SVE_2X, I4XXTORGB_SVE_2X, NVTORGB_SVE_2X, RGBTOARGB8_SVE_2X, RGBATOARGB8_SVE_2X, RGBTORGBA8_SVE_2X, STOREARGB8_SVE_2X, STOREAR30_SVE_2X, and the RGB565/ARGB1555/ARGB4444 2x loops) to process the low and high vector halves consecutively using p1 (0..vl-1) and p2 (vl..2*vl-1) with widening loads + in-lane trn1/trn2 and two contiguous st2h stores ([%[dst]] and [%[dst], #2, mul vl]), removing both st4b and cross-lane zip1/zip2/uzp1/uzp2 permutes.\n\nAcross the 27 affected kernels (1280x720, 1000 iterations), this improves overall performance on Cortex-A510 (SVE2) by 1.22x vs pre-CL (90279 ms -\u003e 74152 ms) and +2.2% vs Patch Set 1 (with +16.9% on I422ToRGB565, +9.0% on I420ToARGB1555, +8.8% on I420ToARGB4444, and +11.4% to +15.3% on I410*), +17.3% vs Patch Set 1 on Cortex-A520 (SVE2), +26.1% (1.35x) vs Patch Set 1 on Lumex C2-Ultra (SME2), and +19.2% (1.24x) vs Patch Set 1 on Lumex C1-Pro (SME2).",
      "parentUuid": "1b404f5b_6a0c8834",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1115,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1115,
        "endChar": 33
